  "plain": "In 1968, Michels says, the physicist Bryce DeWitt wrote a paper about superconductors and gravitational drag. Michels raises it himself while questioning Salvatore Pais, a Navy scientist known for patents on unusual propulsion, and he cites it as a sign that serious physicists were already looking at ways of working with gravity in the late 1960s."
